{
  "_note": "Block textures for voxel scenes. `npm run textures:fetch` downloads each block's first available candidate into src/assets/textures/<key>.png (gitignored, bundled only when present). A block whose file is missing uses its built-in original look. Add a key here, then reference it from a scene. See docs/ASSET_LIBRARY.md. `skins` are 64×64 player skins (src/assets/textures/skins/), `items` are 16×16 item icons (src/assets/textures/items/), used by the Steve character and the sorting board. `npm run build` fetches them first. `mobs` are animal faces cut from Minecraft mob textures (`face` = x,y,w,h in a texture of `size`), or a whole spawn-egg icon; the sorting board uses them for animal icons. `models` are real 3D Minecraft mobs: a Bedrock geometry file (`geo`, picked by `id`) and its texture, from Mojang's bedrock-samples; src/scenes/voxel/mobs.ts builds them.",
